/*
# Gauge

A labeled horizontal value bar: an optional caption, then a rounded track filled to
`value`. It follows the theme like every library control — the fill is the theme's
`accent`, the track its `trackFill`, the caption `textMuted` — and takes a colour of its
own through `tint`. It is for demos and dashboards that want a caption; for a meter with
`min`/`max`, use `ProgressBar`.

```declare
col: View [ x = 20, y = 20, width = 260,
    layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 8 ],
    Gauge [ width = 260, label = "Storage", value = 72 ],
    Gauge [ width = 260, label = "Memory",  value = 38, tint = #37E0C8 ]
    ]
```

## value
How full the track reads, **0–100 always** — a percentage, not your own units. This is
the difference from `ProgressBar`, which takes `min`/`max` and lets you pass raw counts.

## label
The caption to the left of the track. `""` drops the caption column entirely and the
track takes the full width.

## tint
The fill colour: the theme's `accent` unless you give one.

## lead
The caption column's width, derived from whether there is a `label` at all. Set it to
align several bars whose captions differ in length.

## accessibilityLabel
The caption, so a screen reader names the reading as the eye does.

## accessibilityValue
The reading, out of the gauge's fixed 0–100 range.
*/

class Gauge [ height = 28,
    label: string = "",
    value: number = 0,
    tint:  Color  = { provided("theme").accent },

    // a reading out of 100, named by its caption

    accessibilityRole = progress,
    accessibilityLabel = { label },
    accessibilityValue = { value },
    accessibilityMin = 0,
    accessibilityMax = 100,
    lead:  number = { label == "" ? 0 : 96 },
    layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = x ],
    cap: Text [ y = center, width = { classroot.lead }, maxLines = 1, textColor = { provided("theme").textMuted }, text = { classroot.label } ],
    rail: View [ flexes = true,
        height = 100%, cornerRadius = { provided("theme").controlCornerRadius }, fill = { provided("theme").trackFill ?? provided("theme").control },
        bar: View [ height = 100%, cornerRadius = { parent.cornerRadius }, fill = { classroot.tint },
            width = { parent.width * classroot.value / 100 } ]
        ]
    ]
